## Original Content
Apple says it will no longer ditch using its icloud.com domain for hiding people's email addresses.

## Summary
Apple has decided to continue using its icloud.com domain for the Hide My Email feature, preventing its discontinuation. This move ensures that users can still hide their email addresses for enhanced privacy protection.

## Key Points
- Apple rescues the Hide My Email feature from being scrapped.
- The icloud.com domain will remain in use for hiding email addresses.
- This feature bolsters user privacy by allowing email concealment.


